.TH "ET\-MODE" "1" "November 2026" ""
.SH NAME
et\-mode \- select an operating mode for EmComm Tools
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]et\-mode\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]et\-mode\f[R] starts a supported operating mode in EmComm Tools.
.PP
By design, EmComm Tools supports only one radio and one operating mode
at a time.
Close the current mode before selecting another.
.PP
When an operating mode is selected, EmComm Tools resets its managed
services and prepares the system for the new mode.
It performs the following tasks:
.IP "1." 3
Stops all EmComm Tools services and modes that may be running.
.IP "2." 3
Checks that a valid callsign has been configured with
\f[B]et\-user\f[R].
.IP "3." 3
Checks that a radio has been selected with \f[B]et\-radio\f[R].
.IP "4." 3
Checks that the selected radio is connected.
.IP "5." 3
Updates application configuration, including the callsign and detected
audio device, as required by the selected mode.
.IP "6." 3
Starts prerequisite services, such as a modem or packet TNC.
.IP "7." 3
Starts the application for the selected operating mode.
.SH OPERATING MODES
.TP
\f[B]JS8Call\f[R]
Launch JS8Call from its desktop icon rather than through
\f[B]et\-mode\f[R].
EmComm Tools updates the callsign, grid, and audio input and output on
startup.
Other user\-defined settings are preserved.
Enter any portable callsign suffix in JS8Call after it starts.
.TP
\f[B]Fldigi\f[R]
Launch fldigi from its desktop icon rather than through
\f[B]et\-mode\f[R].
EmComm Tools updates the callsign, grid, and audio input and output on
startup.
.TP
\f[B]APRS Client (YAAC)\f[R]
Starts Dire Wolf as a packet TNC and YAAC (Yet Another APRS Client).
A supported GPS receiver is used if connected before the mode starts.
.TP
\f[B]BBS Client (Paracon)\f[R]
Starts Dire Wolf as a packet TNC and the Paracon terminal client for
connecting to packet nodes and bulletin board systems.
.TP
\f[B]BBS Client (QtTermTCP)\f[R]
Starts QtTermTCP for terminal operation and allows the operator to
select which modem to use.
.TP
\f[B]BBS Server (LinBPQ)\f[R]
Starts a 1200\-baud Dire Wolf packet TNC and a LinBPQ packet node
accessible over the tuned VHF/UHF packet frequency as
\f[CR]YOURCALLSIGN\-7\f[R].
The node provides a BBS, chat, YAPP transfers, packet access, and local
management.
The local web interface is at \f[CR]http://localhost:8012\f[R]; sign in
as \f[CR]admin\f[R] using the Winlink password configured with
\f[B]et\-user\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]Chat (chattervox)\f[R]
Starts a 1200\-baud Dire Wolf packet TNC and the chattervox packet chat
client for exchanging messages with stations in range.
.TP
\f[B]APRS Digipeater\f[R]
Starts Dire Wolf as an APRS digipeater using \f[CR]YOURCALLSIGN\-4\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]Packet Digipeater\f[R]
Starts Dire Wolf as a packet digipeater using
\f[CR]YOURCALLSIGN\-2\f[R].
This mode is not intended for APRS operation.
.TP
\f[B]Winlink over VHF/UHF (AX.25 Packet)\f[R]
Starts the Pat Winlink client and a Dire Wolf AX.25 packet TNC.
Pat also listens for inbound peer\-to\-peer (P2P) connections.
.TP
\f[B]Winlink over HF (ARDOP)\f[R]
Starts Pat with the ARDOP modem.
Pat also listens for inbound peer\-to\-peer (P2P) connections.
.TP
\f[B]Winlink over VHF/UHF (VARA FM)\f[R]
Starts Pat with the VARA FM modem when the optional WINE/VARA subsystem
is installed.
This integration requires manual setup and is not part of the standard
plug\-and\-play configuration.
.TP
\f[B]Winlink over HF (VARA HF)\f[R]
Starts Pat with the VARA HF modem when the optional WINE/VARA subsystem
is installed.
This integration requires manual setup and is not part of the standard
plug\-and\-play configuration.
.TP
\f[B]Winlink over FM (xara FM)\f[R]
Starts Pat with the xara FM modem.
This native Linux modem provides VARA FM\-compatible operation with
plug\-and\-play integration.
.TP
\f[B]Winlink over HF (xara HF)\f[R]
Starts Pat with the xara HF modem.
This native Linux modem provides VARA HF\-compatible operation with
plug\-and\-play integration.
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
et\-mode
.EE
.SH WHEN TO RUN
Run \f[B]et\-mode\f[R] when selecting an operating mode or switching
from one operating mode to another.
Close the current mode first.
